<style>
  @page {
    size: A4;
    margin: 0;
  }
  .page {
    width: 794px;
    height: 1123px;
    padding: 50px 60px;
    box-sizing: border-box;
    overflow: hidden;
    page-break-after: always;
    position: relative;
    font-family: "DejaVu Serif", "Liberation Serif", Georgia, "Helvetica", Arial, "DejaVu Sans", "Liberation Sans";
  }
  .page:last-child {
    page-break-after: auto;
  }
  h1, h2, h3 {
    font-weight: bold;
  }
  .section {
    margin-bottom: 20px;
  }
</style>

<div class="page">
  <div style="text-align: center; margin-bottom: 30px;">
    <h2 style="margin: 0;">Oakwood University</h2>
    <p style="margin: 5px 0 0 0;">7000 <span data-field="address.street_number">{{ address.street_number }}</span> <span data-field="address.street_name">{{ address.street_name }}</span>, <span data-field="address.city">{{ address.city }}</span>, <span data-field="address.state">{{ address.state }}</span> <span data-field="address.zip">{{ address.zip }}</span> | Phone: <span data-field="contact.phone">{{ contact.phone }}</span> Fax: <span data-field="contact.fax">{{ contact.fax }}</span> Email: <span data-field="contact.email">{{ contact.email }}</span></p>
  </div>

  <div class="section">
    <h3 style="text-align: center;">HEPATITIS B FACT SHEET</h3>
  </div>

  <div class="section">
    <h3 style="margin-top: 30px;">How common is hepatitis B?</h3>
    <p>One in <span data-field="statistics.prevalence_rate_1">{{ statistics.prevalence_rate_1 }}</span> people now have or will someday contract hepatitis B. Each year about <span data-field="statistics.annual_cases_1">{{ statistics.annual_cases_1 }}</span> Americans are infected, <span data-field="statistics.annual_cases_2">{{ statistics.annual_cases_2 }}</span> die, and <span data-field="statistics.annual_cases_3">{{ statistics.annual_cases_3 }}</span> have chronic hepatitis B infections and are potentially infectious to others. Fifty percent of those infected do not have symptoms but can go on to infect others. About one third do not know the source of their infection. The HBV has shown to remain infectious on environmental surfaces for at least a month at room temperature.</p>
  </div>

  <div class="section">
    <h3 style="margin-top: 30px;">How is hepatitis B spread?</h3>
    <p>Hepatitis B is spread when blood or body fluids of an infected person are absorbed into an individual's blood stream through broken skin or a mucous membrane. The virus can live in all body fluids including blood, saliva, semen, and vaginal fluids. It can enter the body through cuts, tears, or abrasions in the skin and through mucous membranes of the mouth, vagina, anus, and eyes.</p>
  </div>

  <div class="section">
    <h3 style="margin-top: 30px;">Why are college students at risk?</h3>
    <ul>
      <li><span data-field="risk_factors[0]">{{ risk_factors[0] }}</span></li>
      <li><span data-field="risk_factors[1]">{{ risk_factors[1] }}</span></li>
      <li><span data-field="risk_factors[2]">{{ risk_factors[2] }}</span></li>
      <li><span data-field="risk_factors[3]">{{ risk_factors[3] }}</span></li>
      <li><span data-field="risk_factors[4]">{{ risk_factors[4] }}</span></li>
    </ul>
  </div>

  <div class="section">
    <h3 style="margin-top: 30px;">Hepatitis B Vaccine</h3>
    <p>The hepatitis B vaccine is safe and effective. You cannot get the disease from the vaccine. The most common side effect is soreness at the site of the injection. Vaccination requires a series of three shots over a six-month period. After that a booster shot is not necessary. The vaccine protects <span data-field="vaccine_efficacy_percentage">{{ vaccine_efficacy_percentage }}</span> percent of those who complete the three-dose vaccination series.</p>
  </div>

  <div class="section">
    <h3 style="margin-top: 30px;">For More Information</h3>
    <p>The Health & Counseling Services phone number is <span data-field="info.phone">{{ info.phone }}</span>.</p>
    <ul>
      <li>Center for Disease Control (CDC), <a href="http://www.cdc.gov/ncidod/diseases/submenus/sub_hepatitis.htm">{{ info.cdc_link }}</a></li>
      <li>American College Health Association (ACHA), <a href="http://www.acha.org">{{ info.acha_link }}</a></li>
      <li>Immunization Action Coalition (IAC), <a href="http://www.immunize.org">{{ info.iac_link }}</a></li>
    </ul>
  </div>
</div>